/-!
# G.2.3 over larger binary fields

`Hypothesis.lemma_G_2_3` assembles all seven conclusions with the original
marked conjugator. The natural line and Borel calculations give the starred
Sylow subgroup and I=LU. A faithful Sylow lift and transfer eliminate the
central kernel, giving S=WWᵍ. The actual quotient S/S₂ has the asserted marked
direct sum and natural decomposition, and its multiplicity gives the order of U.

The theorem retains only U≤T and Φ(U)≤V₁ from G.2.2 and the universal
G.1.3/G.1.5 recognition implication. The parent §G.2 assembly discharges
these earlier-source inputs. The projective map and every recognition
hypothesis on the literal quotient are constructed here.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004,
G.2.3, printed pp.333–334, PDF pp.344–345.
-/
